# Markdown Style Guide

This document defines markdown formatting conventions enforced by [markdownlint v0.41.1](https://github.com/DavidAnson/markdownlint).

## Enforced Rules

All `.md` files in this repository must pass linting before merge. Use `pnpm lint:markdown` to check and `pnpm lint:markdown:fix` to auto-fix violations.

### Heading & Structure

- **MD003 (Heading style):** Use consistent heading markers (`#`, `##`, etc.). Style is auto-detected from first heading.
- **MD025 (Single H1):** Disabled — allow multiple H1s where needed for fragment files.
- **MD041 (First heading):** Disabled — support config/data files without heading requirement.

### Spacing & Formatting

- **MD004 (Unordered list style):** Use consistent bullet markers (auto-detected).
- **MD007 (List indentation):** Use 2-space indentation for nested lists.
- **MD009 (Trailing spaces):** Disabled — tolerate trailing whitespace in auto-generated content.
- **MD013 (Line length):** Soft limit **160 characters** per line (practical limit for technical documentation, skill headers, and complex structures).
  - Applies to regular text and code blocks
  - **Exceptions:** Tables and headers exempt to preserve complex formatting

### Lists & Links

- **MD024 (No duplicate heading):** Headings must be unique within document siblings (allow within nested sections).
- **MD033 (No inline HTML):** Disabled — allow HTML where markdown equivalents are insufficient.
- **MD040 (Fenced code language):** Disabled — allow unlabeled code blocks for pseudo-code and examples.

### Code & Blocks

- **MD046 (Code block style):** Use fenced blocks (`` ``` ``) not indented (4 spaces).

---

## Quick Fixes

### Check all markdown files

```bash
pnpm lint:markdown
```

### Auto-fix violations

```bash
pnpm lint:markdown:fix
```

### Check a specific file

```bash
pnpm lint:markdown README.md
```

---

## Exceptions & Ignoring Rules

To skip linting for a specific file or section, use HTML comments:

```markdown
<!-- markdownlint-disable MD013 -->
This line can be arbitrarily long without triggering MD013.
<!-- markdownlint-enable MD013 -->
```

Avoid when possible—linting ensures consistency.

---

## CI Integration

CI workflow runs `pnpm lint:markdown` on every PR. Merge blocked until all violations pass. See `.cursor/workflows/lint-markdown.yml` for details.

